# Pairs with LinearizedTerminals. Letting a participant apply a terminal while
# the saga is still merely "prepared" removes the decision-before-broadcast
# ordering, which is the load-bearing linearization of the whole protocol.
MODULE: LinearizedTerminalsBroadcastBeforeDecision
TARGET: LinearizedTerminals
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: lets a participant apply a commit terminal before the registry records the decision

--- FIND
    /\ phase[t] \in {"committing", "aborting"}
    /\ LET kind == IF phase[t] = "committing" THEN "commit" ELSE "abort"
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: broadcast is enabled one phase early, so a leaf can apply a commit
\* terminal while the registry decision is still "inflight". The kind now
\* defaults to commit for any phase that is not an abort.
    /\ phase[t] \in {"prepared", "committing", "aborting"}
    /\ LET kind == IF phase[t] = "aborting" THEN "abort" ELSE "commit"
--- END
